Z||000002||mbramble||10-26-2001||11:40 AM||||It sounds very weird.  But......  I upgraded to IE6 a couple of weeks ago.  All was well in the beginning but at some point it got to where I could not see about 3/4 of the images on web sites.  I found that if I went to View, Encoding and clicked on Western European (even if it ws already selected!) the images would come up -- for that page.  And it is set for Auto select.  Well, it just got very, very annoying.  I tried all sorts of changes to the setting but nothing helped.  Decided to go back to IE5.5 but IE6 would not let me!!  Did a search on yahoo! and came up with a way to de-install IE6.  My previous browser was IE4 (I upgraded to 6 right after I loaded Windows on a new machine)which was reloaded.  Then I just went back to MS and got IE5.5 again.  I'm staying with it for awhile!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieronv||10-26-2001||03:57 PM||||IE6 has a lot of bugs in it and I would recommend uninstalling it for right now unless you are running w2k or xp. You'll be much happier with IE5.5, Also beware of media player7 it can cause similar problems with win98. It is quite easy to remove IE6 from your system just go to the control panel and add/remove programs. Look for explorer and remove it then load from you win disc the previous version of IE. Hope that this helps.||||reg||1
